%h1 User Log Tokens

#application-container
  = show_flashes.html_safe

%p
  Logs and telemetry identify users by an opaque token rather than a raw user id. Each destination gets a different token for the same user, so a token from one system cannot be matched against another's.

%h2 Find a user's tokens

%p.text-muted
  Enter a user id to get that user's token for each destination, then search for it in the corresponding system. This direction reveals nothing you did not already know.

= form_tag url_for(action: 'log_token_form'), method: 'get', class: 'form-inline', enforce_utf8: false do
  = text_field_tag :user_id, params[:user_id], class: 'form-control', placeholder: 'numeric user id', size: 20
  %button.btn{type: 'submit'}
    %i.fa.fa-search

- if @invalid_input
  %p.text-danger Enter a numeric user id.
- elsif @tokens.present?
  - unless @user_exists
    %p.text-muted
      No user currently exists with id #{@input}. The tokens below are still what that id would produce.
  %table.table.table-hover.table-condensed.table-auto-width
    %thead
      %th Destination
      %th Token
    %tbody
      - @tokens.each do |destination, token|
        %tr
          %td= destination
          %td
            - if token
              %code= token
            - else
              %span.text-muted (CDO.user_log_token_keys is not configured in this environment)

%hr

%h2 Identify a user from a token

%p.text-danger
  This re-identifies a student. Every attempt is recorded with your name and the reason you give, whether or not it succeeds, and lookups are rate limited.

= form_tag resolve_log_token_path, method: 'post', enforce_utf8: false do
  %div
    = label_tag :token, 'Token'
    = text_field_tag :token, nil, class: 'form-control', placeholder: 'v1.…', size: 90
  %div{style: 'margin-top: 8px;'}
    = label_tag :reason, 'Reason (required)'
    = text_field_tag :reason, nil, class: 'form-control', placeholder: 'e.g. Zendesk 4821, safety review', size: 60
  %div{style: 'margin-top: 8px;'}
    %button.btn.btn-danger{type: 'submit'} Identify user

- if @resolve_attempted && @resolved.present?
  %table.table.table-hover.table-condensed.table-auto-width
    %thead
      %th User ID
      %th Destination
    %tbody
      %tr
        %td= link_to @resolved[:user_id], permissions_form_path(search_term: @resolved[:user_id])
        %td= @resolved[:destination]

= render partial: 'home/admin'
